Christian genealogy series.
This is the genealogy of Jesus Christ. He is the son of David, and also the son of Abraham.
Abraham was the father of Isaac. And Isaac was the father of Jacob. And Jacob was the father of Judah and his brothers.
Judah the father of Perez and Zerah, and their mother was Tamar. Perez the father of Hezron, and Hezron the father of Ram.
Ram the father of Amminadab, and Amminadab the father of Nahshon, and Nahshon the father of Salmon.
Obaida father of Buz. And Buz father of Obi-El. And El father of Nemuel. And Nemuel father of Shema. And Shema father of Gilead. And Gilead father of Jephthah. And Jephthah father of Ibzan. And Ibzan father of Elkanah. And Elkanah father of Samuel. And Samuel father of David.
And Jesse was the father of King David. And David was the father of Solomon. And the mother of Solomon was the wife of Uriah.
Solomon the son of Rehoboam, the son of Rehoboam the father of Abijah, the son of Abijah the father of Asa.
Asa was the father of Jehoshaphat. And Jehoshaphat was the father of Joram. And Joram was the father of Uzziah.
Uzziah the father of Jotham, Jotham the father of Ahaz, Ahaz the father of Hezekiah.
Hezekiah the father of Manasseh, Manasseh the father of Amon, Amon the father of Josiah.
Hezekiah was the father of Jeconiah and his brothers at the time when the Jewish people were exiled to Babylon.
And afterward the genealogy of the family continued. And Zerubbabel was the father of Shealtiel, and Shealtiel the father of Zerubbabel.
Zerubbabel was the father of Oded. Oded was the father of Eliakim. Eliakim was the father of Azra.
I visit Abu Sadoq. And Sadoq is the father of Akim. And Akim is the father of Eliyahu.
Eliud the father of Eleazar. Eleazar the father of Matan. Matan the father of Jacob.
Jacob was the father of Joseph. Joseph was the husband of Mary. And Mary gave birth to Jesus who is called the Christ.
There were fourteen generations from Abraham to David; and fourteen from David until the carrying away of Babylon the Jews; and fourteen from that time until Christ. The birth of Jesus Christ.
This is how the birth of Jesus Christ came about. His mother Mary was pledged to be married to Joseph. Before they came together, she was found to be with child through the Holy Spirit.
And her husband, Yusuf, was a righteous man. He did not want to expose her to shame among people. So he decided to secretly divorce her.
While he was thinking about these things, an angel of the Lord appeared to him in a dream and said to him, "Joseph son of David, do not be afraid to take Mary your wife into your home, because what is conceived in her is from the Holy Spirit."
She will conceive a son. And you shall call his name Jesus because he will save his people from their sins.
All this happened so that what the Lord had said, and what the prophet had proclaimed, would come to pass.
A young woman who has never known a man will conceive and give birth to a son. She will name him Immanuel. (Isaiah 7:14)
Joseph woke up. He did what the angel of the Lord commanded him. He took Mary into his house as his wife.
But Joseph did not know her until she bore a son, and he called him Jesus.
The Visit of the Wise Men to Jesus
Jesus was born in Bethlehem in Judea. This happened during the time of Herod, the king of Judea. After Jesus was born, Magi from the east came to Jerusalem.
They asked, "Where is the child king who has been born to the Jews? We saw his star when it rose in the east. We have come to worship him."
When Herod the king heard this news, he was deeply disturbed. And all of Jerusalem was disturbed with him.
Herod called the chief priests and the scribes of the people and asked them where the Christ was to be born.
In Bethlehem of Judea, they answered him. This is what the prophet wrote. He said,
And you, Bethlehem Ephrathah, who are little among the thousands of Judah, from you shall come forth to me the one who is to be ruler of Israel, whose origin is from of old, from ancient days.
Herod secretly summoned the Magi and specifically asked them when the star had appeared.
He sent them to Bethlehem and said, "Go and search diligently for the young child. And when you have found him, send me word so that I may also come and worship him."
And after the sages had listened to the king, they went on their way. And the sign which they had seen while they were in the East preceded them, until finally it stood above the place where the boy was.
When they saw the star, they were overwhelmed with joy.
And the wise men went to the house. And they saw the child with his mother Mary. And they prostrated to him and worshipped him. Then they opened their treasures. And they presented to him gold, frankincense, and myrrh.
And God warned them in a dream not to return to Herod, and they returned to their own country by another way. The journey of Jesus's family to Egypt.
And when the assembly had been dismissed, Joseph saw in a dream an angel of the Lord. And he said, "Rise, and take the child and his mother and flee to Egypt, and remain there until I bring word. For Herod is about to search for the child to destroy him."
Joseph awoke from sleep, and departed by night to Egypt with the child and his mother Mary.
They stayed there until Herod the king died. And the word of the Lord which he spoke by the hand of Nathan the prophet, saying, «I will raise up against David my servant a house, and I will establish his kingdom forever. I will also be his father, and he shall be my son. When he does wrong, I will correct him with the rod of men and with the blows of the sons of men. But my loving kindness will not depart from him, as I had covenant with David, my servant. I will also make his house firm forever, and his kingdom shall be exalted forevermore. I will be a father to him, and he shall be a son to me. I will make the place of my feet glorious. All peoples of the earth will see the salvation of God. For he will deliver the needy when he cries for help, the afflicted and the poor, when their life is overwhelmed, in the storm and tempest of life, when the whirlwind sweeps by, and the storm is yet more violent, when the clouds are swifter than eagles, and the tempest is exceedingly great, when the darkness and the light are mingled together, when the white and the black are united, when the red and the pale are made to touch together, when the sickly and the delicate are brought into one, when the strong and the weak are mingled together, when the young and the aged are made to touch one another, when the living and the dead are brought into one, when the quick and the dead are mingled together, when the living and the dead are made to touch one another, when the living and the dead are brought into one, when the living and the dead are mingled together, when the living and the dead are made to touch one another, when the living and the dead are brought into one, when the living and the dead are mingled together, when the living and the dead are made to touch one another, when the living and the dead are brought into one, when the living and the dead are mingled together, when the living and the dead are made to touch one another, when the living and the dead are brought int