Then you will give the charity secretly, for your father sees in secrecy and He rewards you for it. Prayer.
When you pray, do not be like the hypocrites, for they love to pray standing in the synagogues and at the street corners, so that they may be seen by others. Truly, I say to you, they have received their reward.
If you pray, enter your room, close your door, and pray for your father who is in secret; for your Father who sees in secret will reward you.
Do not prattle about prayer as the unbelievers do, thinking that by their volubility they will be heard.
Do not be like them, for your Father knows what you need before you ask Him.
Thus they prayed: "Our Father who art in heaven, Hallowed be thy name."
You are the owner of the heavens and the earth; be your will done on earth as it is in heaven.
Give us this day our daily bread.
Forgive us our trespasses, as we also forgive those who trespass against us.
Make piety beloved to us and save us from trials. Turn the devil away from us and save us from him.
Forgive others when they wrong you, so that your heavenly Father may also forgive you when you wrong.
And if you do not forgive people their slips, your slips will not be forgiven to you. Your father will not forgive your slips, fasting.
If you fast, do not be gloomy-faced like someone who shows off piety. They show faces with frowns as if they are suppressing anger. The veil is taken, they have received their full reward.
But if you fast, anoint your heads with oil and wash your faces.
So do not make them public for the people, and conceal what you have in yourselves. And to Allah is the highest description. And He is the Almighty, the Wise. And when you have prayed, do not be as she who, when death approaches, is in the throes of death.
Do not withhold for yourselves the wealth of the charitable, for the moth corrupts it, the weevil bores it, and the night-time thief breaks in. What their breasts conceal is greater.
Instead, lay up for yourselves treasures in heaven, where neither moth nor rust destroys, and where thieves do not break in or steal.
Your heart will be where your wealth is, wherever you are.
The eye is like a luminous lamp for the body. So if your eyes are enlightened, then your whole body will be luminous.
But if your eye is bad, your whole body will be full of darkness. If the light within you is darkness, how great is that darkness!
No one can serve two masters at the same time. For either he will hate the one and love the other, or he will be loyal to the one and despise the other. You cannot serve both God and Money. Therefore, I tell you, do not be worried about your life, what you will eat or drink, or about your body, what you will wear. Is not life more than food, and the body more than clothing? Look at the birds in the sky; they do not sow or reap, they gather no food, yet your heavenly Father feeds them. Are you not much more valuable than they? Which of you by worrying can add a single hour to his life? And why do you worry about clothing? Consider the lilies of the field, how they grow; they do not toil, they do not spin, yet I tell you, even Solomon in all his glory was not dressed like one of these. If then God so clothes the grass, which is alive today and tomorrow is thrown into the fire, will he not much more clothe you, O you of little faith? So do not worry, saying, 'What shall we eat?' or 'What shall we drink?' or 'What shall we wear?' For the pagans run after all these things, and your heavenly Father knows that you need them. But seek first his Kingdom and his Righteousness, and all these things will be given to you as well. Therefore I tell you, do not worry about your life, what you will eat or drink or about your body, what you will wear. Look at the birds; they do not sow or reap, they gather no food, yet your heavenly Father feeds them. Are you not much more valuable than they? Which of you by worrying can add a single hour to his life? And why do you worry about clothing? Consider how the wild flowers grow; they do not labor or spin. Yet I tell you, not even Solomon in all his splendor was dressed like one of these. If then God so clothes the grass, which is alive today and tomorrow is thrown into the fire, will he not much more clothe you, O you of little faith? So do not worry, saying, 'What shall we eat?' or 'What shall we drink?' or 'What shall we wear?' For the p