The Farmer's Story
On the same day, Jesus left the house and sat on the shore of the Sea of Galilee.
Large crowds gathered around him, so he boarded a boat and sat in it, while all the people stood on the shore.
Then he told them many things, drawing on various stories. He said, "A farmer went out to sow his seeds."
He sowed the seed in the ground. Some of them fell on the road, so birds came and ate them.
Some of the seed fell on rocky places, where there was little soil. And the plants grew quickly because the surface soil is poor.
When the sun rose, it burned the plants. They dried up because they had no roots.
Other seeds fell among the thorns, which grew up and choked the plants.
And some of them in good ground bring forth fruit, going up and increasing: one of them yields a hundred, and another sixty, and another thirty.
